    "structure": "Account Code = Major Head (3 digits) + Minor Head (2 digits) + Detailed Head (2 digits), e.g. 110-01-01.",
    "first_digit_of_major_head": {"1": "Revenue Income", "2": "Revenue Expenditure", "3": "Capital Receipts & Liabilities", "4": "Capital Expenditures & Assets"},
    "mandatory_levels": "Major head = financial-statement level (mandatory, fixed, cannot be added by states). Minor head = schedule level (mandatory; states may ADD minor codes per the manual's logic). Detailed head = state/ULB-defined (illustrative in Appendix 2).",
    "function_dimension": "NMAM keeps FUNCTION (Appendix 1 function codes, e.g. 90 Revenues, 50 Civic Amenities) as a SEPARATE code dimension from the account code. The full budget code strings a Fund code + Function code + Account code together. An income head's city-total therefore aggregates that account code across all function codes; the account code itself is not function-specific. See consolidation note in README.",
    "source": "NMAM 2004, Chapter 4 (Codification Structure), paras 4.20-4.30, pages 4.5-4.7."
  },
